      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional (could be a follow-up CL, since the goto structure comes from the parent CL — but this CL adds another goto site, so it would be reasonable to do here too): the goto exists only because C++ forbids jumping over initializations, and it leaves the failure semantics inconsistent — the first two errors (fp_sensor_get_info() fails, num_types too large) return *without* invalidating, while the per-type errors do. Building into a local array and committing atomically removes the goto and makes every failure path yield an empty cache:\n\n  void FpImageFrameParamsCache::populate_cache(uint32_t max_image_buffer_bytes)\n  {\n  \tframe_params_.fill({}); /* Invalid until fully repopulated. */\n  \t...\n  \tstd::array\u003cFpImageFrameParam, FP_CAPTURE_TYPE_MAX\u003e params{};\n  \tfor (uint8_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c num_types; ++i) {\n  \t\tif (!validate(info-\u003eimage_frame_params[i], max_image_buffer_bytes))\n  \t\t\treturn;\n  \t\tparams[type] \u003d { .frame_size_bytes \u003d size,\n  \t\t\t\t .image_data_offset_bytes \u003d offset };\n  \t}\n  \tframe_params_ \u003d params;\n  }\n\nA small static bool validate(const fp_image_frame_params_v2 \u0026, uint32_t max) keeps the loop body short.",
